# Rakuda visual meshes (53 MB of decorative STL) live in Git LFS and are excluded
# from the wheel. The URDFs and the convex collision meshes are ordinary git files
# shipped as package data, so both a plain clone and `pip install robopy` can run
# the kinematics, the solver and the collision-geometry viewer.
# Fetch the visual meshes with `git lfs pull` (checkout) or `robopy-models fetch` (install).
src/robopy/models/rakuda/assembly_2/meshes/*.stl filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
src/robopy/models/rakuda/assembly_2/meshes/*.STL filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
